The large response is often to an unfinished spelling rather than a pronoun:
'h' + 'err', for example. The previous token locates split spellings;
a short text tail provides coarse language cues. Other positions predict zero.
The short HER-prefix rule excludes 'here' and longer tokens starting with it.
